 adaptive cadence or grant dispatch authority.
+
+### CI identity differential diagnostic
+
+The default-off `--lifecycle-ci-identity-qualification` option admits at most one diagnostic per account per process inside an already-admitted, unchanged, naturally due two-PR CI cohort. Existing watches and individual hints retain their ordinary path. The diagnostic compares two REST candidate identities before and after one GraphQL pair using the same bound credentials, read admission and shared quota, with five transport calls and a fifteen-second aggregate bound. Only stable open, unmerged, mergeable test-merge identities can match; null, unsupported or moving identities remain inconclusive. Probe errors follow normal account cooldown while the outer reservation remains held. Diagnostic facts never replace ordinary source plans, candidate witnesses or CI publication. Existing CI witness batching can remain enabled independently. The diagnostic adds calls for qualification and does not itself reduce requests or establish live compatibility or savings.
